/**
 * @defgroup DoxyG_hazo Hazo
 * @ingroup DoxyG_udho
 * @brief Udho heterogeneous data storage.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup capsule Capsules
 * @brief Capsule serves as an encapsulation of the data inside a node.
 *
 * Some capsules may have a key_type which is used to store associative
 * data. Those capsules call the key() member of the underlying data
 * data structure.
 *
 * The type of the object encapsulated by the capsule is identified
 * as data_type as well as value_type. If the data_type has a member function
 * named value() and a type named value_type, then that type is used as
 * the value_type of the capsule too.
 * @ingroup DoxyG_hazo
 */

/**
 * @defgroup encapsulate Encapsulation
 * @brief Helps encapsulation.
 * @ingroup capsule
 */

/**
 * @defgroup node Nodes
 * @brief Constructs a chain of nodes used for Hazo-based sequences and maps.
 *
 * Each node contains a value of type HeadT and a tail.
 * The terminal node has void tail type.
 * A node internally uses `capsule` to store the data inside the node.
 * @code
 * node<A, node<B, node<C>, node<D, void>>>
 * @endcode
 * @tparam HeadT Type of the value in a node.
 * @tparam TailT Type of the tail (void for a terminal node).
 * @ingroup DoxyG_hazo
 */

/**
 * @defgroup seq Sequences
 * @ingroup DoxyG_hazo
 */

/**
 * @defgroup map Maps
 * @ingroup DoxyG_hazo
 */
